The graph shows the volume $V$ litres of water in a tank over $8$ hours, where $V=60+20t-2.5t^{2}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$t$ (hours)}, ylabel={$V$ (litres)}, xmin=0, xmax=9.5, ymin=0, ymax=125, xtick={2,4,6,8}, ytick={20,40,60,80,100}, samples=100, clip=false, ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:8] {60 + 20*x - 2.5*x*x};
\addplot[only marks, mark=*] coordinates {(0,60) (8,60)};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Use calculus to find the time at which the tank is neither filling nor emptying, and the volume at that time.
